4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T08:47:06-07:00","id":960466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/940248-gming-geist-what-not-to-do?p=940543#post940543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The High Armor from Shroud in 2e is not a problem, but can take you by surprise with it's reliable high numbers.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could you expand on this? How do you handle it? I found quite quickly that someone with the grave dirt shroud was basically invincible unless I started arbitrarily filling buildings with flood waters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T11:51:10-07:00","id":961804,"title":"","content":"So I have the issue of having my players not necessarily bringing their Geists into play much in the Chronicle. I have, as much as possible, brought in situations that would affect their Geists and would cause at least some sort of response from their Geists, however, my players are rather new and I think they forget the fact that they are playing as someone bound with a Geist. Any ideas how I can get them into this habit more inside a chronicle? Or is this something that comes with time? I offered, when we began, three methods to have the Geists interact, Storyteller controls them, Player Controls them, or ANOTHER Player Controls them. They chose themselves wanting to control their Geists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Kinda I want to&quot; - Trent Reznor<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent.ftpa1-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t1.0-9/27973518_2040009129348529_5319855605701568493_n.jpg?oh=9c85c5c9d4a0769a1249ea2f3e62ca43&amp;oe=5B002AA5\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12143-eldritchminister","name":"EldritchMinister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}